    self-loops) yields the min-cost path tree. Every destination uses its
    exact minimum-cost route, and every partition of that destination
    reuses the same route, so per-partition cost equals the per-destination
    minimum. Unreachable destinations (and src itself) get empty paths so
    nothing is transferred for them, keeping every configuration
    successful. Redundant computation is avoided: the shortest-path tree
    is computed once and shared across all destinations and partitions.
